    "response": "{\"decision\":\"established_flaw\",\"issues\":[{\"category\":\"unsupported_inference\",\"target_kind\":\"assertion\",\"claim_quote\":\"Across the whole packet, policy debate follows one dominant pattern shown by the cited source.\",\"evidence\":[{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_f0870e9346a20518\",\"quote\":\"The Home Secretary said that she will make a decision in the autumn, but my right hon. Friend the Member for Leigh (Andy Burnham), my hon. Friends the Members for Liverpool, Walton (Steve Rotheram) and for Halton (Derek Twigg) and I, as chair of the all-party group on the Hillsborough disaster, spent many hours talking with the Home Secretary’s predecessor and the IPCC to...\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_9e53d16449575337\",\"quote\":\"The manifesto we stood on said that the SNP would abolish the House of Lords and replace it with a fully elected second chamber. The motion we are putting forward today gives the Government a slightly more gentle way forward. It does not suggest full abolition at this stage. It suggests making positive changes…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_9d0ced8615915eee\",\"quote\":\"I thank my hon. Friend for that thought-provoking intervention, which will go down in the annals of Hansard. The point was about being out there and seeing what people volunteer to do on our behalf. Accusations are sometimes made about MPs’ foreign travel, but when I told people about signing myself up for a trip to go camping in northern Norway in the middle of winter, it was not…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_0ceca4c893473254\",\"quote\":\"Some 15% of Scottish academics in higher education institutions are EU nationals. That rises to 25% in institutions such as Edinburgh University. Some universities already report having lost advance staff who were due to come from Europe. Will the Minister speak to the Home Secretary and try to get a guarantee of rights for EU staff before we lose any more talent?…\"},{\"excerpt_id\":\"EXC_9d0ced8615915eee\",\"quote\":\"Some 15% of Scottish academics in higher education institutions are EU nationals. That rises to 25% in institutions such as Edinburgh University. Some universities already report having lost advance staff who were due to come from Europe. Will the Minister speak to the Home Secretary and try to get a guarantee of rights for EU staff before we lose any more talent?…\"}],\"whole_packet_no_support\":\"The cited sources discuss diverse policy debates, not a single dominant pattern across the whole packet.\",\"mechanism\":\"The claim conflates isolated statements and interventions with a systemic pattern.\",\"material_consequence\":\"The claim falsely suggests a unified policy debate where none exists, obscuring the specific concerns raised in each excerpt.\",\"counterconditions\":\"The excerpts cover topics ranging from Hillsborough disaster to EU academic staff, demonstrating a lack of a single dominant pattern.\"}],\"unresolved\":[],\"rationale\":\"The evidence demonstrates a fragmented and diverse range of policy discussions, directly contradicting the claim of a single dominant pattern across the entire packet. The claim relies on a forced interpretation of disparate sources.\"}",
